['Here is an example of how you could implement this task using JavaScript and modern features like `async/await` for handling promises and Promises for dealing with external API calls:

```javascript
function createNonce(key) {
    // generate a nonce based on the key
}

async function fetchScriptCode(src, cacheDuration) {
    const cachedResponse = getCachedResponse(src);
    if (cachedResponse && !isExpired(cachedResponse)) {
        return cachedResponse;
    } else {
        const response = await fetch(src);
        const text = await response.text();
        cacheResponse(src, text, cacheDuration);
        return text;
    }
}

async function renderFooterScripts(scriptObjects, config) {
    let footerHTML = '';
    for (const scriptObj of scriptObjects) {
        try {
            const { key, code, src } = scriptObj;
            const nonce = createNonce(key);
            if (src) {
                const fetchedCode = await fetchScriptCode(src, config.cacheDuration || 0);
                footerHTML += `<script nonce="${nonce}">${fetchedCode}</script>\n`;
            } else if (code) {
                footerHTML += `<script nonce="${nonce}">${code}</script>\n`;
            } else {
                console.error(`Both src and code are missing for key: ${key}. Skipping...`);
            }
        } catch (err) {
            console.error(`Error occurred while rendering script for key: ${scriptObj.key}`, err);
            footerHTML += `<script nonce="${createNonce(scriptObj.fallbackKey)}">${config.fallbackScript || ''}</script>\n`;
        }
    }
    document.body.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', footerHTML);
}
```
This function first generates a nonce based on the key of each script object, and then fetches the script code from an external API if available. If no `code` or `src` is provided for a script object, it logs an error message and skips that script object. In case of any error during script rendering, it logs the error and adds a fallback script to the footer HTML string. Finally, it inserts all the generated script tags into the document body using the `insertAdjacentHTML` method.

Please note that you need to implement the caching mechanism for external API responses, as well as any other security measures like CORS settings and rate-limiting based on your application requirements. This code is a basic example and may not be production ready without further adjustments based on specific requirements. 

