["Certainly, here is a very high-level design in C using concepts like pthreads, semaphores etc. Due to the complexity of the task you have mentioned, it would not be possible to fully implement this in one response and without specific business requirements or system context it's hard to give a detailed implementation.

```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <semaphore.h>

typedef struct {
    // Define your log entry fields here
} LogEntry;

typedef struct {
    sem_t lock;
    size_t writeIndex, readIndex;
    LogEntry* buffer;
} CircularBuffer;

void initCircularBuffer(CircularBuffer* cb, size_t size) {
    cb->buffer = malloc(sizeof(LogEntry) * size);
    cb->readIndex = 0;
    cb->writeIndex = 0;
    sem_init(&cb->lock, 0, 1); // binary semaphore for locking
}

void destroyCircularBuffer(CircularBuffer* cb) {
    free(cb->buffer);
    sem_destroy(&cb->lock);
}

// Push a log entry into the circular buffer
void pushLogEntry(CircularBuffer* cb, LogEntry* le) {
    sem_wait(&cb->lock); // lock before modifying data

    cb->buffer[cb->writeIndex] = *le; 
    cb->writeIndex = (cb->writeIndex + 1) % size;

    sem_post(&cb->lock); // unlock after modification done
}

// Pop a log entry from the circular buffer
LogEntry popLogEntry(CircularBuffer* cb) {
    LogEntry le;

    sem_wait(&cb->lock); // lock before reading data

    le = cb->buffer[cb->readIndex]; 
    cb->readIndex = (cb->readIndex + 1) % size;

    sem_post(&cb->lock); // unlock after read done

    return le;
}
```
Please note, this is just a basic circular buffer and a log entry. A fully functional logging system will require a lot more code for handling different external logging services, dynamic service switching, error handling mechanisms, thread safety etc. Moreover, to integrate with JavaScript you might need to use libuv or node-ffi libraries to communicate between C and Javascript.

This is just a basic example to demonstrate how we can create a circular buffer that supports push and pop operations in a multi-threaded environment. A real logging system would require many more components such as log severity filtering, service switching based on availability, performance metrics etc. which goes beyond the scope of this simple C code snippet.
