    auto const results = tcp::resolver(ioc).resolve(host, "80");

    beast::tcp_stream stream(ioc);
    stream.connect(results, ec);
    if (ec) {
        std::cout << "Error: " << ec.message() << "\n";
        return EXIT_FAILURE;
    }

    http::request<http::string_body> req{http::verb::get, "/api/resource", 10};
    req.set(http::field::host, host);
    req.set(http::field::user_agent, BOOST_BEAST_VERSION_STRING);

    http::write(stream, req);

    beast::flat_buffer buffer;
    http::response<http::string_body> res;
    http::read(stream, buffer, res);

    std::cout << "Response: " << res.body() << "\n";
}
```
This is a basic HTTP request in C++ using Boost.Beast library. You would need to expand on this and integrate with other libraries for the full system you described. It's also important to note that creating such a system requires a deep understanding of networking, security, distributed systems, and performance optimization concepts.
