['Below is a basic implementation of the system described:

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.net.*;
import java.io.*;

public class DisjointPairFinder {
    private static final String API_URL = "https://api.example.com/check?number=";

    public List<List<Integer>> findDisjointPairs(int[] arr) throws Exception {
        long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

        UnionFind uf = new UnionFind(arr.length);
        Map<Integer, Boolean> cache = new HashMap<>();
        List<List<Integer>> pairs = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
            if (!cache.containsKey(arr[i])) {
                boolean isUniqueAndDisjoint = validateElementWithAPI(arr[i]);
                cache.put(arr[i], isUniqueAndDisjoint);

                for (int j = 0; j < i; j++) {
                    if (!uf.isConnected(j, i) && !cache.get(arr[j])) {
                        pairs.add(Arrays.asList(arr[i], arr[j]));
                        uf.union(i, j);
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        long endTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
        System.out.println("Total processing time: " + (endTime - startTime) + " ms");

        return pairs;
    }

    private boolean validateElementWithAPI(int num) throws Exception {
        URL url = new URL(API_URL + num);
        HttpURLConnection connection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();

        try {
            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(connection.getInputStream()));
            String responseLine;

            while ((responseLine = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                if (responseLine.equals("true")) {
                    return true;
                } else if (!responseLine.equals("false")) {
                    throw new Exception("Unexpected API response");
                }
            }

            reader.close();
        } catch (SocketTimeoutException e) {
            System.out.println("API call timed out, using cached data");
        } finally {
            connection.disconnect();
        }

        return false;
    }
}
```

This is a simplified implementation that assumes the external API endpoint returns "true" for unique and disjoint numbers and "false" otherwise. It uses a Map to cache the results of previous API calls to reduce redundant requests and improve performance when dealing with large input arrays. The total processing time is measured by subtracting the start time from the end time at the end of the method execution.

The Union-Find data structure has been omitted for brevity, but you can find many online resources that explain its implementation in detail. In a real-world application, proper error handling and optimization would be required to ensure the system scales well as input size grows. Also, logging, caching, or additional feature integration could be added by extending this class or using dependency injection for modularity.
']

