['Here is a rough start on how you could structure your SecureDataManager class in C++. Note that this is a simplified version that requires external libraries (OpenSSL) and won't be able to compile as is, but should give an idea of the overall structure. Also, please note that error handling and cryptographic operations are not implemented here as they require extensive knowledge on how cryptography works, which goes beyond the scope of this question.

```cpp
#include <forward_list>
#include <string>
#include <openssl/evp.h>  // OpenSSL library for cryptography
#include <stdexcept>
#include <iostream>

class SecureDataManager {
private:
    std::forward_list<std::string> data;
    EVP_MD_CTX* ctx = nullptr;  // Context for message digest operations
    OpenSSL_add_all_digests();  // Initialize OpenSSL digests

public:
    SecureDataManager() {
        if(ctx == nullptr) {
            throw std::runtime_error("Failed to initialize cryptographic context");
        }
    };

    ~SecureDataManager() {
        EVP_MD_CTX_free(ctx);  // Free the context when done
    }

    void insertAfterString(const std::string& target, const std::string& newString) {
        auto it = std::find(data.begin(), data.end(), target);
        if (it != data.end()) {  // If found, append after this position
            data.insert_after(it, newString);
        } else {  // Otherwise append to the end of the list
            data.push_front(newString);
        }
    };

    std::forward_list<std::string> getCryptographicFunctions() const {
        std::forward_list<std::string> functions;
        for (auto* m = EVP_get_digestbyname(""); m != nullptr; m = m->next) {
            // If the function is available in this platform, add its name to the list
            if (EVP_get_digests_ex(m)) {  
                functions.push_front(m->name);
            }
        } 
        return functions;
    };
};
```
To fully implement a class with all these requirements would be very extensive and is beyond the scope of this question. However, this should give you a good starting point. Error handling for cryptographic operations, system-specific cryptographic features, performance optimization and resource management are some additional challenges to consider when implementing this kind of functionality in a production environment.
']

