Below is a simple outline of how you might implement the various features required:

```java
public class DynamicMicroservicesOrchestrationEngine {
    // Implementing Service Discovery & Health Monitoring with Eureka
    private EurekaClient eurekaClient;

    public void registerService(String serviceName, String hostname) {
        // Register a new microservice in the Eureka registry
        eurekaClient.register(serviceName, hostname);
    }

    public void deRegisterService(String serviceName) {
        // De-register an existing microservice from the Eureka registry
        eurekaClient.deRegister(serviceName);
    }

    // Implementing Adaptive Load Balancing with Ribbon
    private RestTemplate restTemplate;

    public Object loadBalanceAndInvokeService(String serviceId, String path) {
        // Use the Eureka-aware Ribbon client to choose a suitable microservice instance and invoke it
        return restTemplate.getForObject("http://" + serviceId + "/" + path, Object.class);
    }

    // Implementing Resilience & Fault Tolerance with Hystrix
    @HystrixCommand(fallbackMethod = "reliable")
    public Object invokeServiceWithFallbacks(String serviceId, String path) {
        return loadBalanceAndInvokeService(serviceId, path);
    }

    public Object reliable() {
        // Default fallback method for Hystrix commands
        return new Object();
    }

    // Implementing Rate Limiting & Throttling with Resilience4j
