2. Processing Module: This module will process the data received by the previous module. The module may have to deal with different data formats, so consider making your processing function flexible enough to handle different data types.

3. Transformation Module: This module transforms the processed data into a format that is suitable for storage in your distributed database system. 

4. Storage Module: This module stores the transformed data in your distributed fault-tolerant database system. We can use Redis as it supports clustering and also offers a variety of data types which can be used effectively for storing different types of data.

