6. Error Handling and Retry Logic: Implement error handling strategies that include retry logic with exponential backoff for failed API calls. This will make your application more resilient and less prone to failures due to network partitions or API rate limits.

7. Load Balancing: To distribute the load across multiple worker nodes, you can implement a simple round-robin strategy. Each node in the cluster will process data and then forward it for storage. 

8. Monitoring and Logging: Use a logging library to record runtime information, debug and performance analysis. This is very useful in diagnosing problems later on.

9. Fault Tolerance: Implement failover mechanisms where each service communicates with the other services. If one fails, another can take over and continue processing the tasks. 

10. Eventual Consistency: Use a versioning system to handle conflicts between concurrent updates. This will ensure that your database is always in a consistent state despite multiple nodes trying to update it at the same time.

