['Writing such a complex system requires multiple files and components, which is beyond the scope of this platform. However, I can give you an example code snippet for integrating with one of the logging services using C programming language. The same principles apply to other services as well, but they may require different configurations and authentication mechanisms.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <curl/curl.h>

struct string {
  char *ptr;
  size_t len;
};

void init_string(struct string *s) {
  s->len = 0;
  s->ptr = malloc(s->len+1);
  if (s->ptr == NULL) {
    fprintf(stderr, "malloc() failed\n");
  }
  s->ptr[0] = '\0';
}

size_t writefunc(void *ptr, size_t size, size_t nmemb, struct string *s) {
  size_t new_len = s->len + size*nmemb;
  s->ptr = realloc(s->ptr, new_len+1);
  if (s->ptr == NULL) {
    fprintf(stderr, "realloc() failed\n");
    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
  }
  memcpy(s->ptr+s->len, ptr, size*nmemb);
  s->ptr[new_len] = '\0';
  s->len = new_len;

  return size*nmemb;
}

void sendLogToService(char *log) {
    CURL *curl;
    CURLcode res;

    curl_global_init(CURL_GLOBAL_DEFAULT);

    curl = curl_easy_init();
    if(curl) {
        struct string s;
        init_string(&s);

        curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_URL, "http://example.com");
        curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_WRITEFUNCTION, writefunc);
        curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_WRITEDATA, &s);
        curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_USERPWD, "username:password"); // replace with actual authentication mechanism for the service.

        res = curl_easy_perform(curl);

        if(res != CURLE_OK) {
            fprintf(stderr, "curl_easy_perform() failed: %s\n", curl_easy_strerror(res));
        }

        free(s.ptr);

        curl_easy_cleanup(curl);
    }

    curl_global_cleanup();
}
```
This code snippet is a simple example of how to send logs using libcurl, one of the widely used libraries for making HTTP requests in C programming language. This code doesn't include any error handling or buffering/retry strategies which would be necessary in a production environment. It also uses basic authentication with curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_USERPWD, "username:password"), you need to replace this with actual authentication mechanism for the service.

As for integrating JavaScript and running shell commands asynchronously, it's a bit more involved and would require an additional server-side component (like Node.js). This isn't possible within the same C file due to language limitations. However, in a larger application you could use this JavaScript code:
```javascript
const { exec } = require('child_process');

exec('ls', (error, stdout, stderr) => {
  if (error) {
    console.log(`error: ${error.message}`);
    return;
  }
  if (stderr) {
    console.log(`stderr: ${stderr}`);
