```javascript
function copyBytesFromBuffers(buffersList, numOfBytesToCopy) {
    let totalLength = 0;
    buffersList.forEach(buffer => totalLength += buffer.length);

    if (numOfBytesToCopy > totalLength) {
        throw new Error('Requested number of bytes is more than available in all buffers');
    }

    const newBuffer = Buffer.allocUnsafe(numOfBytesToCopy);
    let copiedSoFar = 0;

    for (const buffer of buffersList) {
        if (copiedSoFar >= numOfBytesToCopy) break;

        const remainingInCurrentBuffer = buffer.length - copiedSoFar;
        const bytesToCopyFromThisBuffer = Math.min(remainingInCurrentBuffer, numOfBytesToCopy - copiedSoFar);

        buffer.copy(newBuffer, copiedSoFar, 0, bytesToCopyFromThisBuffer);
        copiedSoFar += bytesToCopyFromThisBuffer;
    }

    return newBuffer;
}
```

Please note that this is just an outline and does not contain all the necessary details. You would need to fill in the logic for each class, methods and functions as per your requirement. Also you will need to add unit tests and exception handling wherever required to make it production ready code. 

This solution also includes some trade-offs: Ehcache for caching due to its performance benefits over Redis, but at the cost of increased memory usage. The JavaScript function uses `Buffer.allocUnsafe()` which can lead to buffer overflows if not used correctly. These choices were made taking into consideration efficiency, usability and maintainability while prioritizing scalability.
"]

