['Here is the JavaScript code snippet that covers most of your requirements. However, there are certain parts like integrating with external service, WebSocket connections, error handling, caching mechanisms, CORS restrictions, monitoring, alerting system, third-party integration etc., which are complex and need appropriate implementation based on actual application's needs and architecture details. So we only provide a general code for rendering scripts dynamically:

```javascript
// Create the cache to store script data fetched from external service
const scriptCache = new Map();

function generateScriptTag(script) {
    const nonceAttribute = (script.key && script.noncePrefix) ? `nonce="${script.noncePrefix}${script.key}"` : '';
    if (script.src) return `<script src="${script.src}" ${nonceAttribute} type="module"></script>`;
    else if (script.code && script.type === 'text/javascript') return `<script ${nonceAttribute} type="module">${script.code}</script>`;
    else throw new Error('Invalid script object');
}

async function getScriptData(url) {
    // Check if data is in cache, and if so return from cache (to avoid unnecessary API calls)
    if (scriptCache.has(url)) return scriptCache.get(url);

    try {
        const response = await fetch(url);  // Implement handling CORS restrictions here

        // Cache the data to handle redundant requests and enhance performance
        scriptCache.set(url, response.json());
        return response.json();
    } catch (error) {
        console.log('Error fetching script:', error);  // Error handling for script generation & insertion issues
        throw error;
    }
}

async function renderFooterScripts(scripts, config = {}) {
    let html = '';

    for (const script of scripts) {
        try {
            const data = await getScriptData(script.src || config.fallbackScript);  // Dynamically generate nonce attribute based on key property

            // Generate and insert the script tag into HTML string
            html += `${generateScriptTag({...data, ...script})}\n`;  
        } catch (error) {
            console.log('Error rendering footer scripts:', error);  // Gracefully degrade in case of partial failures
        }
    }

    document.body.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', html);
}
```
The above snippet is a basic example and doesn't include all the features you requested, but it should give you a good starting point for creating your `renderFooterScripts` function. Please note that this does not handle WebSocket connections or any form of dynamic configuration updates. Those features would require additional implementation and might be subject to your specific use case, application architecture, etc. 

It's also important to remember to implement proper error handling in a production-level environment. The above code just logs errors to the console for simplicity. In a real-world scenario, you should have more robust logging setup that can send alerts or trigger other actions when an issue arises.
']

