Note: Please replace `config_service`, `logging_service` and `dns_resolution` with actual functions/APIs from your configuration service and DNS resolution libraries. 

1. `init_semaphore()` function to initialize a semaphore:
```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include "config_service.h" // include the header file of your configuration management service
#include "logging_service.h" // include the header file of your logging service

typedef struct {
    pthread_mutex_t lock;
    int value;
} Semaphore;

int init_semaphore(Semaphore* sem) 
{
    if (pthread_mutex_init(&sem->lock, NULL) != 0) {
        log_error("Failed to initialize the mutex");
        return -1; // error code
    }

    int value = config_service_get_value(); // fetch semaphore initialization values from configuration service
    if (value < 0) {
        log_error("Invalid semaphore value fetched from config service");
        pthread_mutex_destroy(&sem->lock); // cleanup on error
        return -1; // error code
    }

    sem->value = value;
    return 0; // success code
}
```
2. `operate_on_semaphore()` function to perform potentially resource-intensive operations:
```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include "logging_service.h"
#include "dns_resolution.h" // include the header file of your DNS resolution library

void operate_on_semaphore(Semaphore* sem, char* hostname) 
{
    pthread_mutex_lock(&sem->lock);

    if (sem->value > 0) {
        // Perform resource intensive operation...

        char ip[16];
        if(dns_resolution(hostname, ip) == 0) 
            log_info("Resolved hostname to IP");
        else 
            log_error("Failed to resolve hostname to IP");

        sem->value--;
    } 
    else {
        log_warn("Semaphore value is less than or equal to zero");
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&sem->lock);
}
```
3. `cleanup_semaphore()` function to release semaphore resources:
```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include "logging_service.h"

void cleanup_semaphore(Semaphore* sem) 
{
    if (pthread_mutex_destroy(&sem->lock) != 0) {
        log_error("Failed to destroy the mutex");
    }

    // Clear other semaphore resources...
}
```
Remember that thread safety and resource integrity should be ensured when developing such modules. Also, you need to use external libraries for DNS resolution and logging service as shown in above code snippets. It's also important to handle errors properly and log relevant information whenever possible. This includes logging at different levels (e.g., info, warning, error), which can help developers identify and troubleshoot issues.
